desc: Filterbank (plonk.studio)
version: 1.2
author: LFSaw
about:
	# filterbank
	A bank of 12 parallel bandpass filters, each with its own frequency,
	gain, resonance (Q) and slope (1-4 cascaded stages).
	Filters are dragged directly in the spectrum view (x = frequency,
	y = gain, mouse wheel = Q), muted individually, edited via a
	right-click menu, or typed in numerically.
	A wideband carries the input signal minus the (gain-scaled) active
	filtered content, so the plugin is transparent by default until the
	wideband is attenuated or muted - filter gains then shape the balance
	between the selected bands and the rest of the spectrum.
	Click a node to inspect/edit it in the panel below the spectrum.
link: https://plonk.studio
provides:
  [nomain] Dependencies/spectrum.jsfx-inc
  [nomain] Dependencies/oversample_upsamplers.jsfx-inc
changelog:
  - Fix 1.1 packaging bug: the "relocate" remap duplicated the category
    folder name, installing to filterbank/filterbank/filterbank.jsfx instead
    of filterbank/filterbank.jsfx. The category folder (derived from this
    file's own location) already places it under plonk toolbox/filterbank -
    no destination remap was ever needed.

import Dependencies/spectrum.jsfx-inc
import Dependencies/oversample_upsamplers.jsfx-inc

slider1:freq1=13.0799<0,100,0.01>-Filter 1 Frequency (%)
slider2:gain1=0<-80,30,0.1>-Filter 1 Gain (dB)
slider3:q1=200<0.1,200,0.01>-Filter 1 Q
slider4:slope1=1<1,4,1>-Filter 1 Slope (stages)
slider5:mute1=0<0,1,1>-Filter 1 Mute
slider6:freq2=16.8251<0,100,0.01>-Filter 2 Frequency (%)
slider7:gain2=0<-80,30,0.1>-Filter 2 Gain (dB)
